# Shown by GitHub as "Cite this repository". The title and authors are repeated
# in the BibTeX entries in README.md and docs/index.md, and the authors in
# pyproject.toml, amorphgen/__init__.py, docs/conf.py and the docs/index.md
# author line: change them together. Update version and date-released with each
# release (test/test_citation.py checks them).
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use AmorphGen in your research, please cite it as below, and also cite
  the interatomic potential you used: the README lists their references.
type: software
title: >-
  AmorphGen: A Python package for amorphous structure generation with
  machine-learning and classical interatomic potentials
abstract: >-
  AmorphGen generates amorphous structure models by melt-quench molecular
  dynamics, by random placement, or by random placement followed by a
  melt-quench anneal, using machine-learning interatomic potentials (MACE,
  CHGNet, SevenNet) or classical potentials, and analyses the resulting
  ensembles.
authors:
  - family-names: Kaewmeechai
    given-names: Chaiyawat
    affiliation: University of Birmingham
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0003-1603-2659"
  - family-names: Slocombe
    given-names: Louie
    affiliation: University of Birmingham
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-6986-5526"
  - family-names: Scanlon
    given-names: David O.
    affiliation: University of Birmingham
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0001-9174-8601"
repository-code: "https://github.com/SMTG-Bham/AmorphGen"
license: MIT
keywords:
  - amorphous materials
  - melt-quench
  - random structure generation
  - molecular dynamics
  - machine-learning interatomic potentials
  - materials science
version: "1.0.0rc4"
date-released: "2026-09-24"
